course: dictionary
lesson: 925
title: Blender: a word with a warning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A blender is an electric kitchen machine with sharp, spinning blades. It chops and mixes food into a smooth liquid, like a smoothie or soup. The words around it give clues: «put it in the blender» and «blend until smooth» show what it does.
explain: The word has a second meaning: anything that blends or mixes things can be called a blender. You may also see «a stick blender» or «a hand blender», which are blenders you hold in your hand. Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Because the blades are very sharp, the sentences around this word also give a warning. «Never put hands or a spoon into a blender while it is running.» Safety is part of what this word teaches you, so always read the warnings carefully.
fact: A blender is an electric kitchen machine with sharp, spinning blades.
fact: «Blend» means to mix things together until they are smooth.
fact: «Blender» can also mean anything or anyone that mixes things.
fact: «Before touching anything inside a blender, switch it off and unplug it, because the blades can start again.»
fact: Keep the lid on while it works, and always ask an adult to help you use a blender.
exercise: In «blend until smooth», what does blend mean? | *To mix until the food is smooth | To cut food into big chunks | To cook food in an oven | To wash the dishes
exercise: What is a blender? | *An electric kitchen machine with sharp spinning blades | A type of bread | A soft bed for a pet | A tool for hanging pictures on a wall
exercise: «Never put hands or a spoon into a blender while it is running.» What should you never do? | Hold the lid on tightly | *Put your hands in while it is running | Put a spoon in while it is running | Ask an adult for help
test: A child is making a smoothie in a kitchen blender. What should happen before she puts her hand near the blades? | *Switch it off and unplug it | Ask a friend to hold the lid | Wipe the blades with a cloth | Take the lid off to look inside
test: Which word means mixing things together until they are smooth? | Chop | Freeze | Pour | *Blend
exam: Read this: «A blender's blades can start again while it is plugged in.» What does this sentence teach us? | Blenders are safe to touch when they are plugged in | Kitchens are always safe places | Blenders only work with fruit | *Blenders can still be dangerous when plugged in, so unplug before touching the blades
